    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nCopper Hill A Landmark Family Residence of Exceptional Scale and Distinction.\n\nPerched at the highest point of Rathmichael Haven and commanding uninterrupted panoramic views across the Irish Sea, Dalkey Island and, on clear days, the coastline of Wales, Copper Hill is a truly remarkable family home. Set amidst approximately 1.37 acres of beautifully landscaped grounds in one of South County Dublin's most prestigious residential locations, this exceptional residence represents the very finest in luxury living, combining elegance, comfort, privacy and outstanding amenities in a setting of extraordinary beauty.\n\nDesigned and constructed by its current owners over two decades ago, the property was meticulously planned as a forever family home, with every detail carefully considered to create a residence that is equally suited to everyday family life and large-scale entertaining. Extending to an impressive scale, the home offers a superb balance of formal and informal living spaces together with eight luxurious bedrooms, creating a residence of rare quality and versatility.\n\nFrom the moment you enter, the sense of grandeur is unmistakable. A bright, double-vaulted entrance hall with a magnificent curved staircase and brushed chrome balustrade creates an unforgettable first impression. The heart of the home is the stunning kitchen and breakfast room, featuring a substantial central island, an extensively equipped pantry that functions as a second kitchen, and direct access to the family room and sun deck. Practical family living is enhanced by a dedicated laundry room with integrated laundry chutes and convenient access to the triple garage.\n\nThe property has been thoughtfully designed around wellness, leisure and entertaining. A spectacular gymnasium with floor-to-ceiling glass doors overlooks the rear courtyard, fountain and play area, while an adjoining steam room and bathroom create a private spa-like experience. The elegant dining room is bathed in natural light through expansive glass doors, while the magnificent drawing room, complete with split-level design and space for a grand piano, opens onto a viewing deck that captures the breathtaking sea views. A beautifully appointed library with antique fireplace provides a peaceful retreat, while two ground-floor ensuite bedrooms and two generously proportioned home offices add further flexibility to the accommodation. Below, a substantial wine cellar, communications room and extensive storage areas complete the lower level.\n\nThe first floor offers some of the most impressive accommodation found in any private residence. A viewing gallery provides a dramatic bird's-eye perspective across the Irish Sea, while the entire southern wing is devoted to an extraordinary principal suite extending to over 2,000 square feet. This private sanctuary comprises a luxurious bedroom, a secondary room suitable as a nursery, dressing room or spa treatment space, two opulent bathrooms and extensive dressing accommodation. One bathroom is accessed through a walk-in dressing room, while the second features a magnificent double Jacuzzi bath complete with integrated champagne bucket and connects to an expansive dressing room lined with bespoke wardrobes.\n\nThe remaining upper-level accommodation is equally impressive, comprising three additional ensuite bedrooms and a magnificent guest suite incorporating a spacious living room, large bedroom, luxurious bathroom and private balcony overlooking the tennis court.\n\nOutside, the grounds are every bit as impressive as the residence itself. Carefully cultivated over many years, the gardens are a horticultural masterpiece featuring specimen trees, herbaceous borders, flowering plants and mature landscaping that create year-round interest and colour. The property's outdoor spaces have been designed to embrace the changing light throughout the day, from spectacular sunrises over the Irish Sea to peaceful sunsets enjoyed from the sheltered rear courtyard. The lunch deck adjoining the family room provides the perfect setting for al fresco dining, while the private tennis court, pavilion and extensive lawns offer exceptional recreational opportunities for family and guests alike.\n\nCombining environmental sustainability with modern comfort, the property benefits from geothermal underfloor heating supported by solar energy, achieving an impressive A-rated BER. Despite its peaceful and secluded setting, the residence enjoys exceptional convenience, with easy access to the M50 motorway network, Dublin Airport and the many amenities of South County Dublin.\n\nMore than simply a house, Copper Hill is a home that has been lovingly created to nurture family life, celebrate special occasions and create lasting memories. As the current owners begin a new chapter following the departure of their grown children, a rare opportunity now presents itself for a new family to acquire one of Dublin's most extraordinary private residences and make it their own.\n\nEarly viewing of this exceptional property is highly recommended."
      },
